      "side": 1,
      "message": "Considering that, I would even prefer to change the versions in jgit, i.e. increase our fork. Let me elaborate:\n\n- With just overruling versions from Gerrit, the version declaration in jgit is misleading, i.e. the apparent BOM does not match what is actually used.\n- We anyway already had the situation that if there was a breaking dependency update, that we had to deal with it (Update the dep in Gerrit or downgrade it in jgit), i.e. the fork should be limited to MODULE.bazel.\n- We already have a specific branch for Gerrit and the bazel build is exclusivele used by Gerrit.\n- Your Option 1 does not work. I actually tested that. As long as there is a MODULE.bazel, bazel will not allow to break module barriers. Might of course be that I have missed something.\n- I would also suggest that we can have a policy to always updated deps in nongoogle.toml if it was updated in jgit, in deps.toml it should at least suggested and if it doesn\u0027t get LC+1 it will be downgraded in jgit.",
