      "writtenOn": "2026-01-18T16:36:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "While further verifying this migration with Gerrit core and custom plugins (such as `gerrit-oauth-provider`), I noticed that Eclipse `.classpath` generation currently breaks for two related reasons:\n\n* The binary JARs for external dependencies are now downloaded into a different output location than before, which means `tools/eclipse/project.py` no longer discovers them correctly and the generated `.classpath` ends up incomplete (or empty).\n* Although `fetch_sources \u003d True` is set, the source JARs are not materialized on disk yet. With `rules_jvm_external`, sources are fetched lazily and only downloaded when something explicitly depends on them. This differs from the previous `maven_jar`-based setup, where source JARs were fetched eagerly and always available.\n\nI have a working prototype that addresses these issues and will follow up with a separate change.",
